{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775392093-Y25rj33JIRAqf8b83ZTL","role":"assistant","created":1775392104,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the raw file, it appears to contain data from multiple Treasury Bulletins (October 1969, January 1970, etc.) all concatenated together. The data for January 1969 is in the first section, but the file appears to include data only up to around late 1969/early 1970.\n\nI need to understand what's in this file more clearly. Looking at the manifest, it says there are source documents from January 1970 through January 1981. Let me check if the file contains that data in some form.\n\nActually wait - I'm looking at the wrong data. The file seems to contain multiple bulletins but I need to search for the specific January data for each year. Let me look at the page files again - maybe I need to look at more page numbers that correspond to the January bulletins.\n\nLooking at the manifest again:\n- January 1970: page 32\n- January 1971: page 24\n- January 1972: page 32\n- January 1973: page 38\n- January 1974: page 37\n- January 1975: page 28\n- January 1976: page 27\n- January 1977: page 27\n- January 1978: page 31\n- January 1979: page 29\n- January 1980: page 30\n- January 1981: page 39\n\nSo the pages I have are: 24, 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 37, 38, 39\n\nThis looks like I have data for all the January bulletins from 1970-1981! But the files are named with \"1969_10\" in them - they must have been extracted from an October 1969 bulletin but contain data for multiple months.\n\nWait, I see that page_32 is mentioned for January 1970 but I already looked at page 32 and it only has data through August 1969. Let me check what the page numbering actually refers to - maybe the page numbers in the manifest don't match what I think.\n\n\nI've examined the page files and discovered they're actually text extracts from different bulletins. Each page covers a specific time period - for instance, page_32 contains federal debt data up to September 1969, while page_37 shows debt subject to statutory limitation through September 1969 as well. The extracted files seem to represent separate sections from various Treasury Bulletins, not just a single document.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_41e4e4012be141a9b4f118be","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Let's extract all January debt figures from the main text file\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1969_10.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nimport re\n\n# Find lines with 'January' and large numbers in a specific pattern\n# Looking for the FD-1 table format: | YEAR-January | Total | Public debt securities | Agency securities | ...\n\nlines = content.split('\\n')\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    # Look for lines with exactly the pattern we saw for January 1969\n    # The format appears to be: | 1969-January | TOTAL | PUBLIC_DEBT | AGENCY_SECURITIES | ...\n    match = re.search(r'\\|\\s*(\\d{4})-January\\s+\\|\\s*(\\d{3},\\d{3})\\s+\\|\\s*(\\d{3},\\d{3})', line)\n    if match:\n        year = match.group(1)\n        total = match.group(2)\n        public = match.group(3)\n        print(f'{year}: Total={total}, Public={public}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
