ry Bulletin would have debt data for that specific January. So I need to extract January debt figures from each respective year's bulletin - January 1969 from the 1969 bulletin, January 1970 from the 1970 bulletin, and so on through January 1980. Since the single file appears to be a compilation, I should look for data organized by year and month within it.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_6f425ae049fd4a08a3155694","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Let's find all unique month-year combinations in the file\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1969_10.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nimport re\n\n# Find all patterns like 'YEAR-Month' or 'YEAR Month'\npatterns = re.findall(r'\\d{4}-(January|February|March|April|May|June|July|August|September|October|November|December)', content)\nprint('Months found:', sorted(set(patterns)))\nprint('Count:', len(patterns))\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
